  "notes": [
    "Asset scope is the complete 3–6 seat physical tabletop and a self-contained declarative state schema; it is not app-wired or a rules engine.",
    "Six reusable player stations expose stack, one double-sided mat, and owner-private disc identity/reserve positions. Hide unused seats for 3–5 players.",
    "The central state JSON carries bid, pass, challenge, flip history, passed-mat position, round wins, elimination and Last Chance lifecycle. The SVG shows a six-entry reveal window; longer histories remain in JSON and must not be truncated.",
    "The six seat pips and slot circles are layout guides, not initialized player identities or claims that pieces are currently present.",
    "Do not replace unknown private disc identity with a guess. Physical stack counts/ordering and face-up values are distinct.",
    "The renderer has no board-wide runtime field for the shared center; `tableZones` and `tableModel` are intentionally self-contained JSON for a later consumer."
  ],
